From: Pass 27 audit session <arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: Fix Miri job: install nightly toolchain robustly (RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN env override)

The Safety-gate job fails for environmental reasons, decoded via an in-job
rustup probe (Pass 27 diag #9/#11): the current ubuntu-latest image makes
`rustup default nightly` ineffective (an environment-level toolchain override,
RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN=stable, outranks `rustup default`; `rustup component add miri`
then targets the effective stable toolchain and fails with "the 'miri' component
which provides the command 'cargo-miri' is not available for the
'stable-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu' toolchain"). Verified twice on live CI that
the install chain exits status 1 with that exact error.

The fix side-steps every selection ambiguity: install nightly with the miri
component in one command and select the toolchain per-invocation with
`+nightly`, whose precedence beats RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN, directory overrides and
the rustup default alike.

Apply with:  git apply docs/audit/F-25-ci-miri-toolchain.patch
(Cannot be pushed from the audit sandbox: the app token lacks the `workflows`
scope — same class as F-20's fetch-depth patch.)
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 13 ++++++-------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -82,12 +82,11 @@ jobs:
       - name: Install Miri
         run: |
-          rustup default nightly
-          rustup component add miri
-          cargo miri setup
+          rustup toolchain install nightly --component miri
       - name: Miri on nros-core
-        run: cargo miri test -p nros-core --lib
+        run: cargo +nightly miri setup && cargo +nightly miri test -p nros-core --lib
       - name: Miri on nros-types
-        run: cargo miri test -p nros-types --lib
+        run: cargo +nightly miri test -p nros-types --lib
